{"hw":"ἀπέχθομαι","html":"<div class=\"lex-entry\"><h4 class=\"lex-hw gk\">ἀπέχθομαι</h4><span class=\"lex-orth gk\">ἀπέχθ-ομαι</span>, later form of <span class=\"gk\">ἀπεχθάνομαι,</span> <span class=\"lex-cite\"> <span class=\"lex-cite-author\">Theoc.</span> <span class=\"lex-cite-scope\">7.45</span> </span>, <span class=\"lex-cite\"> <span class=\"lex-cite-author\">Lyc.</span> <span class=\"lex-cite-scope\">116</span> </span>, <span class=\"lex-cite\"> <cite class=\"lex-cite-title\">AP</cite> <span class=\"lex-cite-scope\">5.176</span> </span> (<span class=\"lex-cite\"> <span class=\"lex-cite-author\">Mel.</span> </span>), <span class=\"lex-cite\"> <span class=\"lex-cite-author\">Plu.</span> <cite class=\"lex-cite-title\">Marc.</cite> <span class=\"lex-cite-scope\">22</span> </span>, etc.; for in <span class=\"lex-cite\"> <span class=\"lex-cite-author\">E.</span> <cite class=\"lex-cite-title\">Hipp.</cite> <span class=\"lex-cite-scope\">1260</span> </span> <span class=\"gk\">ἐπάχθομαι</span> is the better reading; and the <span class=\"lex-gram\">inf.</span> <span class=\"gk\">ἀπέχθεσθαι</span> freq. found in codd. should be written <span class=\"gk\">ἀπεχθέσθαι, ξφ. ἀπεχθάνομαι.</span></div>"}